1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,840
You had me gathering market data
on digital collectibles for so long.

3
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,920
What are you planning to do to Wen Ruosen?

4
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:55,040
Take a look at this.

5
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:59,040
WEN RUOSEN, FOUNDER OF YUANZHOU GALLERY

6
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,320
I already know all this.

7
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:02,480
He used to be your mentor,

8
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,240
and you worked under him for quite a while
before you left the firm.

9
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,800
Do you know why I left Boen?

10
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:10,720
Back then,

11
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:12,880
Wen Ruosen screwed me over badly.

12
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:17,840
Back then, he was only a junior partner,

13
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,040
and I was a young consultant

14
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:21,360
who looked up to him wholeheartedly
like an elder brother.

15
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,280
Boen landed the transformation project
for Jingshang Department Store.

16
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:26,480
He led the team and drafted a plan
to turn Jingshang Department Store

17
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,920
into a chain brand.

18
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,040
But halfway through the project,

19
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:32,880
he realized the plan
was ill-suited for local conditions

20
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,880
and would definitely lead
to massive losses down the line.

21
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,720
So he suddenly promoted me to PM.

22
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,520
At that time, I thought I was so lucky,

23
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,760
like a thoroughbred steed
spotted by a discerning talent.

24
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:47,560
Little did I know, he promoted me just…

25
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:50,080
To save his own skin
and to make you take the fall?

26
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,360
Exactly.

27
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,600
Less than two months after the handover,

28
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,080
Jingshang Department Store hit disaster.

29
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:56,280
It was a treasured,
time-honored enterprise

30
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,680
with 60 years of history.

31
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,960
Boen's reputation was ruined overnight.

32
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:01,880
Luckily, the internet
wasn't as widespread back then.

33
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,480
The headquarters spent
an eight-figure PR budget

34
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,280
to contain the scandal.

35
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,880
As the project manager,

36
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,480
I had to resign.

37
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,080
But what about Wen Ruosen?

38
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,120
Didn't he bear any responsibility?

39
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,840
He left hundreds of Jingshang employees
jobless and destitute.

40
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:22,640
But I couldn't stand him tricking me
into taking the fall,

41
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:24,560
ruining all those people's lives,

42
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,600
and walking away scot-free.

43
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:30,880
Later, he even wrote me
a glowing recommendation letter.

44
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:33,760
For a time, I was deeply grateful to him.

45
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:35,480
Later,

46
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:38,200
after I applied
to every consulting firm in Beijing

47
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,320
and got rejected by all of them,

48
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:43,600
it suddenly dawned on me.

49
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,520
So you were…

50
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:49,560
You're trying to say
I was naive and foolish.

51
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,600
I've always wondered

52
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,640
what you were like
when you were naive and foolish.

53
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,560
Go ahead, take a look.

54
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,760
So you moved to Shenzhen afterwards?

55
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:22,360
Back then, I lost nearly everything.

56
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,640
Yet I refused to give up so easily.

57
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:28,160
Up north, most firms were foreign-owned,

58
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,200
so I decided to try my luck
in the Pearl River Delta.

59
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,280
Plenty of enterprises
were growing wildly there,

60
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:36,320
alongside many homegrown
consulting firms rising rapidly.

61
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:37,560
I revised my resume,

62
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:40,120
erased my work experience at Boen,

63
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,680
and joined a mid-sized company
with Hong Kong capital backing.

64
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:43,600
MILK TEA, BEEF TRIPE, DESSERT HOUSE
TEAROOM, STREET FOOD

65
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,960
<i>I kept grinding away</i>

66
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,960
<i>and gradually built up</i>
<i>a bit of a reputation.</i>

67
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,080
<i>That's when I met Du.</i>

68
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,000
<i>He recruited me</i>
<i>to start a venture together.</i>

69
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:52,320
<i>Later I found out</i>
<i>Du had also been screwed over</i>

70
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:54,040
<i>by Wen Ruosen, just like me.</i>

71
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:58,000
<i>What's more, his father</i>
<i>was a long-time employee at Jingshang.</i>

72
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:00,600
<i>Wen Ruosen cost all of them their jobs.</i>

73
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:03,120
<i>Victims deserve compensation.</i>

74
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,000
<i>Wen Ruosen has to pay the price,</i>
<i>just like I did.</i>

75
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,080
<i>It took me two years</i>

76
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,280
<i>to finally land a project</i>
<i>for a major American brand</i>

77
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,200
<i>launching in China.</i>

78
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,680
<i>I even won the Constantine Award.</i>

79
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,600
The Constantine Award?

80
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:16,160
The highest honor from
the International Consulting Alliance?

81
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,520
It was only silver,

82
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,200
but I finally had the money
to compensate the victims from Jingshang.

83
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:22,440
I also earned my way back
into the top consulting circle.

84
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:26,160
After that, I joined P&amp;J
to gain hands-on operational experience.

85
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:29,480
Then I moved to Hezong.

86
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,760
That was when you interviewed me?

87
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:35,560
That was our first meeting.

88
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:40,920
So what was I like in your eyes back then?

89
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,640
Some kid who knew nothing
yet tried hard to pretend to be an elite?

90
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,280
Back then, you were

91
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,480
a pretty proud, promising young woman.

92
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,880
You shone bright.

93
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:56,040
I was just thinking.

94
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,760
By having me do all this work,

95
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:58,920
are you trying to set a trap for him?

96
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,640
Yes.

97
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,480
But doesn't he have any defenses at all?

98
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,560
He screwed you over before.
He must know what he did.

99
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:07,200
Over all these years,

100
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:08,480
he's hurt so many people.

101
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,480
He can't even keep count.

102
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:11,720
And after so many years,

103
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,760
he's long rationalized
all the terrible things he did.

104
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:16,080
By now, he probably thinks
what he did back then

105
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,360
was no big deal at all.

106
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:21,240
Anyway, I send him text messages
on every holiday.

107
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:23,360
And when we meet,
I'm always grateful to him.

108
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:27,080
I think he's got no defenses at all.

109
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:30,800
You're such a crafty old fox.

110
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:35,800
Alright.

111
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:38,600
From now on, I'll call you Officer Rabbit.

112
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:46,280
Officer Rabbit will definitely help you
take Wen Ruosen down.

113
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,480
Just tell me what exactly I need to do.

114
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,400
You've already done it.

115
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,000
Look at this.

116
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,640
YE XINZHI: WHEN ARE YOU GOING
TO GIVE ME MY PITCHFORK?

117
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:11,280
MESSAGE

118
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,240
WEN RUOSEN

119
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:13,240
WEN RUOSEN: SAW YOUR POSTS. YOU
AND MR. DENG FROM MORSE KNOW EACH OTHER?

120
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,320
YE: YEAH, WE'VE KNOWN FOR SIX, SEVEN YEARS

121
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,360
WEN: YOU TWO PRETTY CLOSE?
HE EVEN ASKED YOU TO PLAY SPORTS

122
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,400
YE: WE GET ON OKAY, I SUPPOSE
FIRST MET AT THEIR COMPANY ANNUAL DINNER

123
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,400
YE: WE'VE WORKED ON A FEW PROJECTS

124
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,480
WEN: GOOD FOR YOU
ANY COLLABORATION RECENTLY?

125
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,440
WEN: ANY IDEA HOW INTERESTED THEY ARE
IN THE METAVERSE NEW ECONOMY?

126
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,400
YE: FAIRLY INTERESTED. THEY BACKED XINHONG
IN Q1 FOR BLOCKCHAIN SMART CONTRACTS

127
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:22,640
You're setting a trap.

128
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:25,080
Don't say anything. Let me guess.

129
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,120
Wen Ruosen's Yuanzhou Digital Collectibles

130
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:32,320
is essentially a reseller
for high-priced digital collectibles.

131
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,960
Since the collections he represents

132
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,680
are works by renowned artists,
they carry sky-high valuations.

133
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,880
But the business
has never turned a profit.

134
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,440
Wen Ruosen is drowning in debt.

135
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,320
If he wants to keep maintaining
those high valuations,

136
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:42,840
he needs to create new business scenarios.

137
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:45,920
Benyuan Digital Collectibles,
which we ran into at the forum last time,

138
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,480
is Hong Kong's largest
digital collectibles platform.

139
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:50,360
That's why Wen Ruosen kept trying
to persuade them to take a stake.

140
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:53,160
But their cooperation
has been going nowhere.

141
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,200
Did you do something behind the scenes?

142
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,160
I had you gather plenty of information
on Benyuan Digital Collectibles,

143
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,320
asked Du to prepare
several rounds of free financial analysis

144
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:01,520
for Yong'an Trust,

145
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:03,680
the major investor of Benyuan,
and Yong'an pulled out.

146
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:06,240
So Wen Ruosen has to look
for other funding sources.

147
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,600
In fact, he approached Morse before,

148
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:10,920
but got nothing out of it.

149
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,520
He found that I've recently
been working closely with Morse

150
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,640
on the Tianhe Air project,

151
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,720
so he came to me.

152
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:18,200
He wants you to broker
financing with Morse.

153
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:21,280
He is holding a digital collectibles
exhibition on Thursday night.

154
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,160
I invited Mr. Deng on his behalf.

155
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,640
They will have an in-depth talk then.

156
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:28,600
However, I've been working
for Morse lately,

157
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:29,800
so there are things I can't talk about.

158
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:36,000
That's why I'll work on your behalf.

159
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:38,400
You're the irreplaceable, shining

160
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,640
Officer Rabbit and girlfriend.

161
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:52,320
‎Mr. Ye, what have you been up to lately?
‎I haven't seen you in a while.

162
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,640
‎I've been busy putting together a wedding.

163
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:55,560
‎Oh.

164
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,160
-Hello.
-Hi.

165
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,280
Please come in.

166
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,280
Hi.

167
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:06,920
Long time no see.

168
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,360
After the event,
shall we grab a drink together?

169
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:13,000
No. My partner won't be happy about it.

170
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,160
Hi.

171
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:25,000
What did she just say to you?

172
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,680
She told me

173
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,280
she wanted to ask me out
for a drink after the event.

174
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:32,600
I said, "Sorry, I'm afraid my partner
would be upset."

175
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:44,160
-Who is your partner?
-You.

176
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,800
I told you not to buy it.

177
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,080
Now we're late, right?

178
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:51,880
They've arrived. I'll greet them.

179
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:54,120
Are you really upset?

180
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,760
I said I didn't want to buy it,

181
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,840
-but you insisted on buying it now.
-What took you two so long?

182
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:59,440
It's all his fault.

183
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:01,400
Right after work,
he said we hadn't had dinner

184
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,640
and couldn't drink here.

185
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:05,040
Then he parked the car at
the convenience store to buy a sandwich.

186
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,400
And guess what? We got a ticket.

187
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,040
Haven't you known him long enough?

188
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:12,080
He was worried about you.

189
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:16,360
Chi knows me best.

190
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,440
Keep an eye on him.
Don't let him go off the rails.

191
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:23,080
I have no sway over him.

192
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:28,280
But someone's coming after you.

193
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,600
Hello, Mr. Ye.

194
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:53,200
Miss Bu, I've heard so much about you.

195
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,280
My turn. Master Ye.

196
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:04,400
I'm Xu Chi's good buddy
and Tianna's close friend.

197
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:07,480
I've studied
all your classic consulting cases.

198
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:09,960
Just call me Richard.

199
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:11,600
As Chi's boyfriend,

200
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:13,720
I appreciate you looking after her
so well at Maxmise.

201
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:16,520
Chi is mine.

202
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,760
It's only natural for me
to look after her.

203
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,000
No need for you to be polite.

204
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:24,680
‎Hey.

205
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:27,040
Excuse me. Du is over there.
I have to take my leave.

206
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,040
Bye-bye.

207
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:36,480
You just stole his line.

208
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:39,320
Chi already said they've known each other
since college.

209
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,120
What business was it of mine?

210
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,360
He comes after me.

211
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,120
Help me touch up my makeup.

212
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,360
What's going on between you two?

213
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:54,080
Why did you suddenly ask me
to this exhibition?

214
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:56,240
You were so mysterious on the phone.

215
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:57,920
And your outfit…

216
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,440
What's wrong with my outfit?

217
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:02,040
You don't look like
you are under investigation

218
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:03,240
for suspected financial issues.

219
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:04,960
You look like you're here to take photos.

220
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:07,120
Actually, you'd look great
in photos wearing this.

221
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,960
Then take one for me. Here.

222
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:10,920
Come on.

223
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,480
What's going on? Spill it.

224
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:15,800
He has a side project,

225
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:17,680
but he can't show up in person.

226
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:19,560
Since I'm free now,
I'm just helping him out.

227
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:21,040
Are you two really together?

228
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:31,920
But is there no risk of you
working on that side project for him?

229
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:33,960
He strung you along before,

230
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:36,240
but now he's preying on you.

231
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,160
This is a romance scam.

232
00:12:38,680 --> 00:12:40,600
I know you're worried about me,
but trust me.

233
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,320
I can judge this for myself, okay?

234
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:47,080
How much judgment can a woman
in love possibly have?

235
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:48,480
I know that too well.

236
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:56,040
He brought me here today,
and without the slightest hesitation,

237
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,400
announced to everyone
that I'm his girlfriend.

238
00:12:57,480 --> 00:13:00,040
Meanwhile, they're still investigating me.

239
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,320
Do you know what this means?

240
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:06,960
It means he's staking his own reputation
in the consulting circle to vouch for me.

241
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:10,000
That alone is tremendous support for me.

242
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,600
Your matter will surely be fine.

243
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:16,760
Now you should enjoy yourself
while you're on leave.

244
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:18,800
Once you get through this ordeal,

245
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,920
you'll be back at Maxmise working hard.

246
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,440
He's always off on business trips,

247
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:24,400
and you'll be pulling
all-nighters at work.

248
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,640
Even if you manage to set up a date,
you'll have to cross-check your schedules.

249
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:27,640
Let me tell you,

250
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:30,600
even over a candlelit dinner,
you'll get four or five work calls.

251
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,800
It'll be absolutely miserable.

252
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,280
Absolutely miserable?

253
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:39,160
So you've imagined
this scene many times in your head?

254
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,880
With who?

255
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:49,200
Alright.

256
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:52,040
You said you wanted to broaden
your network beyond your dad.

257
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:53,920
I'll introduce you to a few people today.

258
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,600
Let's go.

259
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:58,880
Take it slow.

260
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:05,600
He actually knows people here?

261
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:09,920
He doesn't seem to be happy.

262
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,320
Although now Zhao Heng

263
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,440
flies all over the place
and stays at high-end hotels,

264
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,600
he was remarkably frugal
when he was a student.

265
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:18,840
-I think it was during undergrad, right?
-Yes.

266
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,120
We went to the US
for a summer camp together.

267
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:22,360
He and I took direct flights,

268
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:24,440
but this guy transferred for over 40 hours

269
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:25,760
just to save a few hundred US dollars.

270
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:27,000
-Right?
-Yeah.

271
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:28,320
-I'm not mistaken, am I?
-Back in school,

272
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,680
I wanted to save some money.

273
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,440
This guy was not only thrifty,

274
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:33,040
but also great at making ends meet.

275
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:35,120
-Back then, we stayed in…
-A homestay.

276
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,120
Yeah, a homestay.

277
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,840
The meal plan was included,
70 US dollars a month.

278
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:38,840
-We all signed up for it.
-Yeah.

279
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:39,760
Only he didn't.

280
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:43,400
He took the bus to discount supermarkets
and bought these huge bags of bread.

281
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:44,800
Without even any jam.

282
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,080
Back then, I made a bet with him.

283
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:49,360
I said, as the summer camp
lasts two months,

284
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:51,040
he couldn't stick to plain food every day.

285
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:52,680
And guess what happened?

286
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:54,720
-Mexican restaurant, right?
-Mexican restaurant, yeah.

287
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,280
He collected leftover duck necks

288
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:59,160
and chicken feet from there
and braised them in a pot.

289
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,440
It smelled amazing that day!

290
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,120
I still remember that taste.

291
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,640
No wonder when I saw you
from afar just now…

292
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:05,960
-Keep your poser company,
-I didn't recognize you just now.

293
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,040
-and I'll go and check.
-Couldn't even place your name.

294
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,840
Two duck necks
instantly popped into my head.

295
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,640
When will you braise for us again?

296
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:12,560
Sure, I'll make it for you.

297
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,960
Alright, how about

298
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:15,840
I change my WeChat avatar
to two duck necks later?

299
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:17,680
-Okay, it's a promise.
-Don't you dare.

300
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:21,480
Your WeChat avatar
has to be a photo I pick.

301
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,760
Who even are they?

302
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:42,240
They don't even know me,
yet they dare come to a place like this.

303
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,240
They're my college classmates.

304
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,240
We were roommates.

305
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,560
College classmates?

306
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:51,280
Your college roommates still don't know
you braised duck necks in the US

307
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:53,040
because I love them?

308
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:55,880
Honey, stay away from them.

309
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,440
You're being so childish.

310
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:59,160
For us women,

311
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:00,680
when people take our kindness
for weakness,

312
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:02,120
acting all chummy to our faces

313
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:04,400
yet dripping with subtle sarcasm
and making sly digs at me,

314
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,120
I'd have exposed them all over
WeChat Moments long before.

315
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,240
I…

316
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,920
Alright, less arguing.

317
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:16,600
Tianna and I are going over there
to greet some friends. You folks chat.

318
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,720
-It's fine. Go ahead.
-Go on.

319
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:20,200
Let's go.

320
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:23,960
You're in my way.

321
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:30,840
Be right back.

322
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,120
She's got what it takes.

323
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:36,040
That bag is a limited edition.

324
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:38,240
-I saw through it at once.
-No wonder.

325
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:39,760
Come here.

326
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:41,720
Fix my hair.

327
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:44,440
Fix my hair! Hurry. They're watching.

328
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:51,720
Aren't you such a charmer?

329
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:53,160
Bring out all those tricks
you used to pursue me.

330
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:57,440
Come closer to me.

331
00:16:57,520 --> 00:17:00,040
How come you're stunned
after hearing what they said?

332
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:29,720
Your earring is crooked.

333
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:33,200
What are you thinking?

334
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:45,480
Gentle.

335
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,320
They are still watching.

336
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:55,520
Thank you.

337
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,600
I used to fight alone out there.

338
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,880
This is my first time being protected.

339
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,120
It feels sweet.

340
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,080
So nice.

341
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,600
Fighting alone?

342
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:23,680
I wonder what lousy places
you used to go to.

343
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,600
That's why you got intimidated
the second you came here.

344
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,400
Obviously, you get bullied by them,
yet you were grinning foolishly.

345
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:31,200
It's okay.
With you protecting me, I fear nothing.

346
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,480
Why would I protect you?
What exactly are we to each other?

347
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:37,640
We're just colleagues.

348
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,920
You're colleagues with Chi too,
and you protect her as well.

349
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:42,240
Well, I… I…

350
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,680
Speak of the devil.

351
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,000
She's waving at us.

352
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:48,760
Let's go.

353
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:53,120
Mind your manners.

354
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:56,800
Didn't you teach me that?

355
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:58,040
Let's go.

356
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:02,360
-That's wonderful.
-Yeah.

357
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:03,520
-I saw this last time.
-You saw it last time.

358
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,880
-We've talked about it.
-Right.

359
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:05,800
Hello.

360
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:07,360
-Let's shake hands. Come on.
-Hello, Mr. Deng.

361
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:08,680
Hello. You look stunning.

362
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,440
Hope you'll get the chance
to work together in the future.

363
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:11,760
Sure.

364
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:14,280
This lady looks very familiar to me.

365
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,040
-Long time no see.
-Long time no see.

366
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:18,040
Hello.

367
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:19,880
-Any new work recently?
-This is your…

368
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,000
My father.

369
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:23,280
Which firm does he…

370
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:25,240
Excuse me. I need to step away.

371
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:26,160
Carry on.

372
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:32,840
-Nervous?
-A little.

373
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,280
Take a deep breath.

374
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,120
Let's go over our plan again.

375
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,560
You work behind the scenes,
I take the stage.

376
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:42,560
We'll act as intermediaries,

377
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,480
brokering financing
between Wen Ruosen and Morse.

378
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:48,160
But we'll advise Morse
to set extremely demanding wager terms.

379
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:51,560
If Wen Ruosen wants the investment,
he has to stake everything he owns.

380
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:53,080
Because your analysis shows

381
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:55,120
that risks in the digital collectibles
market have built up to a high level.

382
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,560
Once in a recession,

383
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:58,200
market values will plummet
across the board.

384
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:01,080
By then, Wen Ruosen will definitely
lose this wager.

385
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,480
One question.

386
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:07,040
What if we introduce them to each other,

387
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,720
and they cut us out to negotiate directly?

388
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,240
That won't happen.

389
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:12,880
Then they'd break the rules.

390
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:14,520
Besides,

391
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:17,120
they haven't known each other
long enough to trust each other.

392
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:20,320
Wen Ruosen desperately needs capital.

393
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:23,840
If he wants to push the financing process
forward efficiently and quickly,

394
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:25,960
he has to use a third party like us.

395
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:29,000
Simply put, this is a small-scale
financing consultation.

396
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:31,440
Okay. One more thing.

397
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:35,040
If Yuanzhou Gallery really blows up,

398
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:36,920
will we end up hurting Morse and Mr. Deng?

399
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:40,040
Absolutely not.

400
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:42,400
We're facilitating a transaction,

401
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,800
not fabricating anything.

402
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:47,480
As one of the world's
most experienced investment banks,

403
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:49,200
Morse has their own
professional evaluation models.

404
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,840
So even if our plan works,
nothing bad will happen to Deng.

405
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,000
Sure,

406
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:56,440
I hope Wen Ruosen reaps what he sows soon.

407
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:59,840
But I'm not some bloodthirsty monster
who will stop at nothing just for revenge.

408
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,040
I can be the monster too.

409
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:07,520
You're the beauty, and I'm the beast.

410
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:11,320
Can't you stop joking at a time like this?

411
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:13,920
You're not nervous anymore.

412
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:18,560
Now,

413
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,240
it's your time to shine.

414
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,240
-Hello.
-Xinzhi.

415
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:27,000
-Sir.
-Miss Xu.

416
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:28,200
-Mr. Wen.
-This is Mr. Deng.

417
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:29,720
-Hello, Mr. Deng.
-Hello.

418
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:41,280
Alright, I've got the general picture.

419
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:44,240
Since Richard recommended this,
I'll make sure to arrange it properly.

420
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:47,600
It wasn't Richard, but Miss Xu.

421
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:49,840
My memory's failing me.

422
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:53,000
I forgot Richard is busy with the project
between Tianhe Air and us.

423
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:54,960
He can't get involved in other projects.

424
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:58,320
Miss Xu is the matchmaker
for this project.

425
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,240
Yes, that's right.

426
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:00,880
She's been on leave recently.

427
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,280
I'm glad you don't mind her
limited experience

428
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,520
and are willing to mentor her.

429
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:04,920
I won't stand on ceremony.

430
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:06,680
No need to stand on ceremony.

431
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:08,000
Let's celebrate.

432
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:09,920
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

433
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:12,320
-Happy cooperation.
-Happy cooperation.

434
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:17,920
I'm worn out.

435
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:49,600
I can do it myself.

436
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:51,640
Take the other one off too.

437
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,600
Just relax. You've had a tough day.

438
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:18,320
I'm fine.

439
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:19,880
I've got you here.

440
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,320
What are you laughing at?

441
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:34,200
I just had a really childish thought.

442
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:37,240
I wish time could freeze
right at this moment.

443
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:44,960
Sure. I'll cast my magic.
Give me your hand.

444
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:51,240
Close your eyes.

445
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:53,760
Let's feel it together.

446
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,600
Alright, it's done. The magic ends.

447
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,120
Already?

448
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:00,720
Barely a moment.

449
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:03,400
It's enough.

450
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:07,880
You've already given me more than enough.

451
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:12,520
Actually, during the reception today,

452
00:25:13,120 --> 00:25:14,840
I felt everything was so surreal.

453
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:18,920
Thank you.

454
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:21,760
Back there, in front of Tianna,
you saved me plenty of face.

455
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:25,920
You introduced her to so many people
and looked out for Zhao Heng.

456
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:31,160
Tianna didn't say anything out loud,
but she's grateful deep down.

457
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:32,760
She is from the Bu family.

458
00:25:32,840 --> 00:25:35,640
Isn't she totally at home
at events like this?

459
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:37,160
Why would she need my introduction?

460
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,240
That's not the case.

461
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:41,320
Today she wasn't there
as the eldest daughter of the Bu family,

462
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:44,320
but as Bu Tianna.

463
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:50,800
You're what matters most.

464
00:25:52,560 --> 00:25:53,400
How did you find today?

465
00:25:56,320 --> 00:25:59,720
I think today was amazing.

466
00:26:00,440 --> 00:26:01,400
I mean it.

467
00:26:01,920 --> 00:26:06,800
It feels like I'm holding
a thread in my hand,

468
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:10,440
and I'm carefully gathering
pearls of all different shapes.

469
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:15,160
Someday I'll turn them
into a dazzling necklace.

470
00:26:15,760 --> 00:26:16,640
Really.

471
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:19,200
I think if our goal this time
weren't to take Wen…

472
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,280
The weather is nice outside.

473
00:26:31,360 --> 00:26:32,560
How about going for a walk out there?

474
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:34,280
My feet don't hurt anyway.

475
00:26:34,840 --> 00:26:35,920
Alright.

476
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:39,800
Don't be mad.

477
00:26:40,320 --> 00:26:42,320
I was thinking

478
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:44,920
that if our goal this time
weren't to take Wen Ruosen down,

479
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:46,000
but to truly expand and strengthen

480
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,040
Yuanzhou Digital Collectibles
through financing,

481
00:26:48,120 --> 00:26:49,760
it'd have been quite interesting.

482
00:26:51,520 --> 00:26:55,360
Sometimes I was also thinking
that if Wen Ruosen got lucky,

483
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:57,560
or the regulatory policies
hadn't come out so soon,

484
00:26:58,200 --> 00:26:59,800
I would have helped him.

485
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:01,840
But there's no way around it.

486
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:03,920
Since I chose an open scheme,

487
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:05,560
I can't change the strategy.

488
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:08,680
If you like financing consultation work,

489
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,600
I can take you on more deals later.

490
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,240
Great.

491
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:17,680
If we close this deal for them,

492
00:27:17,760 --> 00:27:21,080
will we get this
according to industry rules?

493
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:24,360
For a favor deal like this,

494
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:26,080
if it were to succeed,

495
00:27:26,640 --> 00:27:28,000
no less than 1%.

496
00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:30,400
That would cover the down payment
for your mother's apartment.

497
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:33,360
I remember everything you've said.

498
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:36,880
But watch my wording.

499
00:27:36,960 --> 00:27:38,440
If it were to succeed.

500
00:27:38,520 --> 00:27:39,760
The subjunctive mood.

501
00:27:40,320 --> 00:27:42,520
So, we both need to work hard.

502
00:27:51,560 --> 00:27:53,280
I will do my best

503
00:27:53,360 --> 00:27:57,120
because this is my first chance
to follow you

504
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:59,920
and do a full project
from start to finish.

505
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:03,480
I have to prove
that I'm qualified and capable

506
00:28:03,560 --> 00:28:04,840
of standing behind you
and working with you.

507
00:28:06,080 --> 00:28:08,320
Not behind, but beside.

508
00:28:25,920 --> 00:28:28,000
<i>Last time I made the first move.</i>

509
00:28:28,080 --> 00:28:30,720
<i>This time it's up to you.</i>

510
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:51,320
<i>I wish time</i>
<i>could freeze right at this moment.</i>

511
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:52,640
Give me your hand.

512
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:54,120
Close your eyes.

513
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:56,400
<i>Let's feel it together.</i>

514
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:07,760
<i>He means it.</i>

515
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:26,000
<i>Still nothing.</i>

516
00:29:28,720 --> 00:29:30,120
<i>Then I'm leaving.</i>

517
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,720
I'm heading back.

518
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:11,320
What consultant rests this early?

519
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:13,000
That's so unprofessional.

520
00:30:13,760 --> 00:30:16,960
I want to talk to you
about the plan for Wen Ruosen.

521
00:30:25,480 --> 00:30:26,640
Sure.

522
00:30:27,280 --> 00:30:29,960
Then, Richard,

523
00:30:30,040 --> 00:30:32,320
may I come over to your place
to work overtime on the plan?

524
00:30:33,400 --> 00:30:34,640
Of course you can.

525
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:36,800
I've got some fine red wine at home.

526
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:38,480
We can work while drinking red wine.

527
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:41,720
Work while drinking?

528
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:46,640
No.

529
00:30:47,200 --> 00:30:48,640
I… I was joking.

530
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:51,600
You see, no one's
at my place during the day.

531
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:54,120
There's a printer, and the sofa is comfy.

532
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:57,400
I hope you can work comfortably
when working for me.

533
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:07,000
Is that okay?

534
00:32:12,640 --> 00:32:14,760
I can't accept this reason.

535
00:32:14,840 --> 00:32:17,400
Vincent, if you think
I'm easy to push around,

536
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:18,960
then it'll end here.

537
00:32:22,040 --> 00:32:23,160
You're back.

538
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:24,880
Let's leave it at that.

539
00:32:24,960 --> 00:32:25,800
We'll be in touch.

540
00:32:28,880 --> 00:32:31,200
Sorry. I made such a mess here.

541
00:32:31,280 --> 00:32:32,200
It's fine.

542
00:32:32,720 --> 00:32:33,880
But what happened to you?

543
00:32:33,960 --> 00:32:35,680
Why did you suddenly blow up
at Wen Ruosen?

544
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:39,720
He thinks the proposal we offered
is far too harsh.

545
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:40,880
He even changed

546
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:42,920
just two figures
in the documents we prepared

547
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:44,760
and went to other small investment funds,

548
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:46,080
trying to get them to agree.

549
00:32:46,160 --> 00:32:48,520
Then he'd use that
to pressure Morse and us.

550
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:51,400
Why get so upset over this?

551
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:54,160
Didn't we expect this before?

552
00:32:54,760 --> 00:32:55,800
I know.

553
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:57,240
Du passed this news to me.

554
00:32:58,400 --> 00:33:00,160
You said Wen Ruosen would

555
00:33:00,840 --> 00:33:03,000
hit a wall and come back,

556
00:33:03,080 --> 00:33:05,120
so I poured oil on that fire,
and I lost my temper with him on purpose.

557
00:33:06,360 --> 00:33:07,200
I threw the documents

558
00:33:07,280 --> 00:33:09,280
to make the background drama
sound convincing.

559
00:33:10,080 --> 00:33:11,760
As a steady, seasoned partner,

560
00:33:11,840 --> 00:33:13,440
you definitely wouldn't abandon
the whole matchmaking deal

561
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:15,080
just because of minor setbacks.

562
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,480
But I'm different.

563
00:33:16,560 --> 00:33:18,280
I'm an impulsive young girl.

564
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:20,440
If I fly off the handle and pull out,

565
00:33:20,520 --> 00:33:22,640
he won't get funding from either side
and will be more anxious.

566
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:24,920
It was an act.

567
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:26,880
You really took a big risk.

568
00:33:28,040 --> 00:33:29,560
Don't worry.

569
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:31,480
I know exactly what I'm doing.

570
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,560
I checked his natal chart.

571
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:34,960
He's a Libra,

572
00:33:35,040 --> 00:33:36,480
with the Moon in Capricorn.

573
00:33:36,560 --> 00:33:38,800
So when big issues come up,
he's bound to hesitate.

574
00:33:39,640 --> 00:33:41,640
Suspicious, yet craving control.

575
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:43,520
I even looked up his MBTI. He…

576
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:45,320
You rely on horoscopes
for matters like this?

577
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:51,400
But I think PDP behavioral testing
is much the same as horoscopes.

578
00:33:53,600 --> 00:33:55,720
Fine, let me put it another way.

579
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:57,400
He has a chameleon personality.

580
00:33:57,480 --> 00:33:58,720
He blows with the wind.

581
00:33:58,800 --> 00:34:00,440
He seems bold on the surface,

582
00:34:00,520 --> 00:34:01,720
but deep down, he's really timid.

583
00:34:01,800 --> 00:34:03,480
That's why I'm pulling a hard move.
It might work wonders.

584
00:34:04,160 --> 00:34:07,600
I just greeted you on purpose
to let him hear us.

585
00:34:07,680 --> 00:34:10,800
I guess he must be
in a real fluster right now.

586
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:12,880
He'll probably call you
shortly to sound you out.

587
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:26,239
WEN RUOSEN

588
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:28,440
See? I was right.

589
00:34:29,199 --> 00:34:31,800
Hang up on him.
Two minutes later, call him back,

590
00:34:31,880 --> 00:34:33,840
tell him you were calming me down,
and reproach him a little.

591
00:34:35,320 --> 00:34:36,400
Hang up.

592
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:40,480
Just do as I say this time. Please.

593
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:46,520
Thank you.

594
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:51,000
She was overly emotional just now.

595
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:52,360
I really couldn't take the call.

596
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:54,040
It's my fault.

597
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:56,400
I didn't expect her to have
such a fierce temper.

598
00:34:56,480 --> 00:34:57,680
<i>I've embarrassed you.</i>

599
00:35:01,920 --> 00:35:04,240
Mr. Wen, about this matter,

600
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:05,320
let me say something.

601
00:35:05,400 --> 00:35:07,480
You moved a bit too hastily on this.

602
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:11,000
Financing has lead and follow-on
investment roles.

603
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:14,000
<i>We'd nearly</i>
<i>got everything lined up for you.</i>

604
00:35:14,600 --> 00:35:17,760
Why did you bypass us
and go through all this trouble?

605
00:35:18,800 --> 00:35:19,720
It wasn't like that.

606
00:35:20,240 --> 00:35:22,560
They thought Morse
was going to invest in me,

607
00:35:22,640 --> 00:35:24,760
so they pestered me
with all kinds of questions.

608
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:27,320
<i>That's what made Miss Xu misunderstand.</i>

609
00:35:29,240 --> 00:35:32,360
Yes. I just said a couple
of words on your behalf,

610
00:35:32,440 --> 00:35:33,880
and she sent me out onto the terrace.

611
00:35:34,840 --> 00:35:36,760
As I told you before,

612
00:35:37,960 --> 00:35:40,760
she had a tough time at Maxmise.

613
00:35:41,360 --> 00:35:45,080
<i>So I brought her here to let her unwind</i>

614
00:35:45,160 --> 00:35:48,360
and to see if Chi and I can help you.

615
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:50,640
It's my way to repay
your support back then.

616
00:35:51,800 --> 00:35:53,280
But as things stand,

617
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:58,640
maybe Chi and I
should withdraw from this project.

618
00:35:58,720 --> 00:36:01,440
No. You mustn't do that.

619
00:36:01,520 --> 00:36:02,400
It's a minor misunderstanding.

620
00:36:03,440 --> 00:36:04,360
Yes.

621
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:15,000
<i>Well?</i>

622
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:18,320
<i>This truly is my bottom line.</i>

623
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:21,240
Alright, I understand.

624
00:36:21,320 --> 00:36:24,720
Well, I'll try to persuade Chi later.

625
00:36:25,240 --> 00:36:26,680
If it falls through,

626
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:28,880
I'll do my best to negotiate
with Deng on your behalf.

627
00:36:28,960 --> 00:36:30,000
Okay?

628
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:33,040
Okay, thank you.

629
00:37:17,680 --> 00:37:19,600
Your appointment letter.
I nearly forgot it.

630
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,880
I was planning to fetch it myself.

631
00:37:23,960 --> 00:37:25,480
Didn't expect you'd bring it over.

632
00:37:25,560 --> 00:37:26,680
By the way,

633
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:28,600
the Academic Affairs Office
assigned me a course.

634
00:37:29,120 --> 00:37:31,160
Strategic Analysis.
The first class is next Saturday.

635
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:33,280
Great, that's wonderful.

636
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:34,760
Everything will fall into place.

637
00:37:35,640 --> 00:37:38,240
Now all matters are proceeding as planned.

638
00:37:39,200 --> 00:37:40,400
How about Wen Ruosen?

639
00:37:41,600 --> 00:37:42,640
He took the bait.

640
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:45,800
So we're three months
ahead of our original plan?

641
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:46,640
Yes.

642
00:37:47,280 --> 00:37:49,120
He basically accepted
the terms I drafted for Morse.

643
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:52,160
Morse will subscribe to 38% equity
of Wen Ruosen's Yuanzhou.

644
00:37:52,240 --> 00:37:54,080
Yuanzhou promises a minimum
25% compound annual growth rate

645
00:37:54,160 --> 00:37:55,240
in performance.

646
00:37:55,840 --> 00:37:57,520
Failing that, Wen Ruosen
shall repurchase all shares

647
00:37:57,600 --> 00:37:59,480
at a compound annual interest rate of 13%.

648
00:38:01,240 --> 00:38:03,200
Twenty-five percent won't work at all.

649
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:04,840
Initially, we set it at 40%.

650
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:07,040
The digital collectible market
is red-hot right now.

651
00:38:07,120 --> 00:38:09,720
What if he tries hard
and actually hits over 25%?

652
00:38:09,800 --> 00:38:11,520
Then we'd end up helping him.

653
00:38:12,720 --> 00:38:13,880
This is all he promised.

654
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:15,560
But Chi added one clause to the agreement

655
00:38:15,640 --> 00:38:18,600
that Morse accepts market value
fluctuations within normal ranges.

656
00:38:18,680 --> 00:38:22,400
Yet the lower bound for the normal range
in the addendum is set at minus 30%.

657
00:38:22,480 --> 00:38:26,280
Namely, if Yuanzhou Digital Collectibles
drops to 70% of its market value,

658
00:38:26,360 --> 00:38:28,320
the company's full ownership
will transfer to Morse.

659
00:38:30,920 --> 00:38:33,200
That girl really delivered.

660
00:38:33,280 --> 00:38:35,000
Has nobody from their team
found out about this?

661
00:38:35,080 --> 00:38:36,280
They haven't.

662
00:38:36,360 --> 00:38:38,040
They were totally wrapped up

663
00:38:38,120 --> 00:38:39,880
in arguing whether
the performance commitment

664
00:38:39,960 --> 00:38:41,480
should be 25% or 40%.

665
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:42,880
When I went to pick up Chi,

666
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:44,440
I noticed Wen Ruosen's back was soaked.

667
00:38:45,040 --> 00:38:46,840
His legal team
was chugging Red Bull nonstop.

668
00:38:47,440 --> 00:38:48,280
With this tactic,

669
00:38:48,360 --> 00:38:49,760
she wore them down completely,

670
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,000
leaving them no bandwidth
to check anything else.

671
00:38:56,160 --> 00:38:58,200
I wouldn't call him authoritative,

672
00:38:58,280 --> 00:39:00,480
but everyone does reference his data.

673
00:39:00,560 --> 00:39:01,480
Yeah.

674
00:39:06,640 --> 00:39:07,480
What…

675
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:10,320
What's this?

676
00:39:11,720 --> 00:39:13,600
Have you two already…

677
00:39:15,440 --> 00:39:16,800
We had.

678
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:22,280
You old dog, nice work.

679
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:25,240
At the reception that night,
I thought you were putting on an act.

680
00:39:25,320 --> 00:39:26,440
Come on.

681
00:39:26,520 --> 00:39:29,080
Every time you see me,
all we talk about is work.

682
00:39:29,160 --> 00:39:30,880
Why didn't you update me on such big news?

683
00:39:30,960 --> 00:39:32,080
How far have you gotten?

684
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:33,880
Actually, not that far.

685
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:37,920
The moment I saw her with another man,

686
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,320
I knew I was done for.

687
00:39:40,360 --> 00:39:43,960
Your tone doesn't sound right.

688
00:39:44,040 --> 00:39:46,320
With your capability,
you fear you can't control her?

689
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:51,000
Not exactly. But she's changed me a lot.

690
00:39:51,920 --> 00:39:55,520
So are you worried she's too sharp,

691
00:39:55,600 --> 00:39:56,840
or…

692
00:40:01,320 --> 00:40:04,160
<i>For instance, I thought</i>
<i>I'd observed Wen Ruosen long enough</i>

693
00:40:04,240 --> 00:40:05,640
<i>to know him inside out.</i>

694
00:40:05,720 --> 00:40:10,480
<i>So I kept spinning the net step by step,</i>
<i>hoping to slowly trap him.</i>

695
00:40:11,320 --> 00:40:12,200
‎-Xinzhi.
‎-Sir.

696
00:40:12,280 --> 00:40:13,960
-Miss Xu.
-This is Mr. Deng.

697
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:15,760
-Hi, Mr. Deng.
<i>-I checked his natal chart.</i>

698
00:40:15,840 --> 00:40:17,200
He's a Libra.

699
00:40:17,280 --> 00:40:18,320
<i>Yet I never imagined</i>

700
00:40:19,040 --> 00:40:21,040
<i>Chi would use horoscopes and MBTI,</i>

701
00:40:21,120 --> 00:40:24,000
<i>things I used to dismiss,</i>
<i>to analyze his character.</i>

702
00:40:24,080 --> 00:40:25,680
<i>And she actually got him right.</i>

703
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:26,840
You rely on horoscopes?

704
00:40:26,920 --> 00:40:28,720
If you think I'm easy to push around,

705
00:40:28,800 --> 00:40:30,240
then it'll end here.

706
00:40:31,760 --> 00:40:34,080
<i>Later, without letting me know,</i>

707
00:40:34,160 --> 00:40:36,000
<i>she blew up on purpose</i>

708
00:40:36,080 --> 00:40:38,240
<i>and broke through</i>
<i>Wen Ruosen's psychological defenses.</i>

709
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:40,880
You said Wen Ruosen would

710
00:40:40,960 --> 00:40:43,920
hit a wall and come back eventually,
so I poured oil on that fire,

711
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,360
and I lost my temper with him on purpose.

712
00:40:45,440 --> 00:40:46,720
<i>Well?</i>

713
00:40:46,800 --> 00:40:48,720
<i>This truly is my bottom line.</i>

714
00:40:50,120 --> 00:40:51,360
Alright, I understand.

715
00:40:51,440 --> 00:40:52,920
Okay, thank you.

716
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:57,040
<i>The second Wen Ruosen</i>
<i>agreed to accept Chi's terms,</i>

717
00:40:57,120 --> 00:41:00,600
<i>I even asked myself</i>
<i>whether I'd fallen behind</i>

718
00:41:00,680 --> 00:41:03,720
<i>and lost the sharp insight</i>
<i>I once prided myself on.</i>

719
00:41:05,760 --> 00:41:07,640
Of course I'm not scared
of her growing more capable.

720
00:41:08,320 --> 00:41:11,760
I truly hope
she can fly higher and higher.

721
00:41:11,840 --> 00:41:13,280
After all, she's immensely talented.

722
00:41:14,360 --> 00:41:15,560
Lots of her moves and ideas

723
00:41:15,640 --> 00:41:17,240
surpass what I can comprehend.

724
00:41:18,520 --> 00:41:20,840
She fills me with a deep respect
for the younger generation.

725
00:41:23,760 --> 00:41:25,720
You've had it far too easy
over these years.

726
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:26,840
Everything went smoothly for you.

727
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:28,760
You've never faced any setbacks. Right?

728
00:41:28,840 --> 00:41:29,720
Now you're facing setbacks.

729
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:31,360
Whether you like to hear it or not,
I'm going to say it.

730
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:32,520
You're…

731
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:34,560
You're just too solitary.

732
00:41:34,640 --> 00:41:36,240
You struggle to trust others.

733
00:41:36,760 --> 00:41:38,360
It took us
four or five years working together

734
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:40,280
before we opened up to each other.

735
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:43,040
Now you've met a girl
whom you can't get control.

736
00:41:43,120 --> 00:41:45,200
No wonder you're lost.

737
00:41:46,360 --> 00:41:48,520
Deep down, you think
she liked you at first

738
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:50,400
because she looked up to you.

739
00:41:50,480 --> 00:41:52,080
But now that you're dating, growing close

740
00:41:52,160 --> 00:41:54,240
and seeing each other plainly,

741
00:41:54,320 --> 00:41:55,520
the mystery fades,

742
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:58,400
and your untouchable aura is gone, right?
